<section class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 py-16">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6 text-center">YouTube Video Thumbnail Download Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-center mb-10">Last updated: <%= currentYear %></p>

    <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        YouTube thumbnails are the preview images that represent a video. They are useful for presentations, design inspiration, archiving your own content, and creating reference boards. This guide explains how to download YouTube thumbnails in all available sizes.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Available YouTube thumbnail sizes</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li><strong>Default (120x90):</strong> Small preview, low resolution.</li>
        <li><strong>Medium (320x180):</strong> Standard quality preview.</li>
        <li><strong>High (480x360):</strong> Better quality for most uses.</li>
        <li><strong>Standard (640x480):</strong> Older default, may not be available for all videos.</li>
        <li><strong>Max Resolution (1280x720):</strong> Full HD thumbnail when the uploader uploaded a high-quality image.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">How to download a YouTube thumbnail</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Copy the YouTube video URL.</li>
        <li>Go to <a href="/thumbnail" class="text-sky-600 dark:text-sky-400 hover:underline"><%= siteTitle %> Thumbnail Downloader</a>.</li>
        <li>Paste the URL and solve the captcha.</li>
        <li>Preview all available thumbnail sizes.</li>
        <li>Click the <strong>Download</strong> button under the size you need.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Using thumbnails legally</h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">You can freely download thumbnails for videos you own. For other creators' videos, use thumbnails only for personal reference, education, or commentary. Republishing or editing thumbnails without permission may violate copyright.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Tips for creators</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
        <li>Upload custom thumbnails at 1280x720 for best quality.</li>
        <li>Use clear text and high contrast to attract clicks.</li>
        <li>Keep the file size under 2 MB for YouTube upload.</li>
        <li>Use JPG, PNG, or GIF formats for thumbnails.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white mt-8 mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Can I download thumbnails in HD?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Yes, if the creator uploaded a 1280x720 custom thumbnail. Otherwise the highest available size is shown.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Do I need a YouTube account?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">No. Public video thumbnails can be downloaded without logging in.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">Can I use a thumbnail for my own video?</summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Only if you created it or have permission. Using someone else's thumbnail can be copyright infringement.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
